    Last week, our local library's digital app crashed right when the most-awaited memoir dropped, leaving everyone unable to download their borrowed e-books. It was a frustrating glitch that showed how much we rely on these digital bridges. A server sync error left thousands of readers waiting in limbo. Fortunately, the team worked overnight to restore the connection and clear the cache. By Saturday morning, the holds were moving and the stories were flowing again. Digital access is fragile, but the infrastructure behind it is resilient.

